# arbiter — Gitleaks suppression list
# Managed by arbiter. Do not remove this file.
#
# MANDATORY FORMAT: every suppression fingerprint MUST be immediately preceded by
# a metadata comment in this exact format (pipe-separated, single line):
#
#   # reason: <10+ chars — include a tracking issue URL> | owner: @github-handle | expiresAt: YYYY-MM-DD | scope: commit-hash-or-all
#   <fingerprint-or-commit-hash>
#
# Rules enforced by scripts/check-suppressions.mjs on every L1 commit:
# - All four fields (reason, owner, expiresAt, scope) are mandatory
# - expiresAt must be a future date — expired entries block the gate
# - Warnings appear for entries expiring within 30 days
# - There are no permanent suppressions — max recommended expiry: 12 months
#
# To add a suppression:
# 1. Run: gitleaks detect --report-format json | jq '.[].Fingerprint'
# 2. Add the metadata comment immediately before the fingerprint
# 3. Set expiresAt to when the fixture/test secret will be removed (≤12 months)
# 4. Reference the tracking issue in reason
#
